  "limitations": [
    "The comparison uses current maintained source with recent optimizations disabled versus enabled; it does not rebuild an older release.",
    "Both arms use default modified Euler and ordinary renewable modified-Euler/double-precision states without converter iteration-voltage memory. Older staggered-solver timings are not directly comparable.",
    "Both keep the quarter-cycle step, 1e-5 complex voltage-correction tolerance, two fresh-solve minimum iterations, 50 maximum, current-P/impedance-Q loads and complete output.",
    "Cases use separate sequential JVMs because current-handoff eligibility is static at class initialization. Case order is before/after for Case 1 and after/before for Case 2. CPU affinity and all settings are pinned; measurements are not interleaved in one JVM.",
    "Residual compilation is included in all measurements. All five measurements and their compiler counters are retained; no isolated minimum or time subtraction is substituted.",
    "The existing PSS2A helper is unclassified by the conservative frequency selector; both cases retain all 2000 frequency measurements. No frequency-selection or passive-bus skipping gain is exercised.",
    "All 36 warmup/measured recordings are complete and repeatable within their profile; each profile also matches its complete pilot. Both event sides and negative-time startup history remain.",
    "The default-Euler full-profile paths change finite-tolerance results. Optimized rotor-angle RMSE against the tighter internal control is 0.0757756761 and 0.0254792322 degrees, above 0.01 degrees. Case 1 voltage NRMSE also exceeds 0.005.",
    "Tighter internal controls establish neither independent reference accuracy nor approval of the profile as a new production default. No engine source or production configuration is changed.",
    "Failed harness compilation/qualification and missing numerical-package analysis attempts are retained, separately from completed simulation results."
  ],
